.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH bhtune-tune 1  "bhtune-tune "
.SH NAME
bhtune\-tune \- Run an MRFT tune against a real OPC DA loop or the in\-process simulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbhtune\-tune\fR [\fB\-\-cycles\-skip\fR] [\fB\-\-cycles\-count\fR] [\fB\-\-noise\-protection\-secs\fR] [\fB\-\-bridge\-host\fR] [\fB\-\-server\fR] [\fB\-\-sim\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-sim\-tau\fR] [\fB\-\-sim\-dead\-time\fR] [\fB\-\-sim\-noise\fR] [\fB\-\-sim\-seed\fR] [\fB\-\-sim\-initial\-pv\fR] [\fB\-\-sim\-initial\-mv\fR] [\fB\-\-pv\-range\-high\fR] [\fB\-\-pv\-range\-low\fR] [\fB\-\-mv\-range\-high\fR] [\fB\-\-mv\-range\-low\fR] [\fB\-\-direction\fR] [\fB\-\-notes\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-write\-pid\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-tagname\fR> <\fB\-\-template\fR> <\fB\-\-process\-type\fR> <\fB\-\-controller\-type\fR> <\fB\-\-relay\-amp\fR> <\fB\-\-driver\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run an MRFT tune against a real OPC DA loop or the in\-process simulator
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-tagname\fR \fI<TAGNAME>\fR
PV tag prefix; the rest of the tag set is derived from it using `\-\-template`\*(Aqs suffix convention. Ignored for `\-\-driver simulator`, which uses two fixed internal tag names instead
.TP
\fB\-\-template\fR \fI<TEMPLATE>\fR
DCS/PLC template name (see `bhtune template list`)
.TP
\fB\-\-process\-type\fR \fI<PROCESS_TYPE>\fR

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
flow
.IP \(bu 2
pressure\-line
.IP \(bu 2
pressure\-vessel
.IP \(bu 2
level
.IP \(bu 2
temperature\-mixing
.IP \(bu 2
temperature\-heat\-exchange
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-controller\-type\fR \fI<CONTROLLER_TYPE>\fR

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
p
.IP \(bu 2
pi
.IP \(bu 2
pid
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-relay\-amp\fR \fI<RELAY_AMP>\fR
Relay amplitude, as a percentage of the MV range
.TP
\fB\-\-cycles\-skip\fR \fI<CYCLES_SKIP>\fR
Relay cycles to skip before counting begins (default: looked up per `\-\-process\-type`)
.TP
\fB\-\-cycles\-count\fR \fI<CYCLES_COUNT>\fR
Relay cycles to count once the skip period ends (default: looked up per `\-\-process\-type`)
.TP
\fB\-\-noise\-protection\-secs\fR \fI<NOISE_PROTECTION_SECS>\fR
Seconds a switch must persist before it\*(Aqs accepted (default: looked up per `\-\-process\-type`)
.TP
\fB\-\-driver\fR \fI<DRIVER>\fR
Which driver drives this tune
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
opcda: A real OPC DA server, reached through an opcda\-bridge gateway
.IP \(bu 2
simulator: The in\-process FOPDT simulator — no external dependency at all
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-bridge\-host\fR \fI<BRIDGE_HOST>\fR
opcda\-bridge gateway address. bhtune connects to the bridge gateway rather than a DCOM host directly — see AGENTS.md\*(Aqs OPC DA integration notes. Only meaningful with `\-\-driver opcda` (default: `crate::config::DEFAULT_BRIDGE_HOST`, overridable via the `BHTUNE_BRIDGE_HOST` env var or the config file\*(Aqs `bridge_host` key)
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR \fI<SERVER>\fR
OPC DA server ProgID (legacy: `\-s`/`\-\-opcServerID`). Required with `\-\-driver opcda`
.TP
\fB\-\-sim\-gain\fR \fI<SIM_GAIN>\fR [default: 1]
Simulator process gain (`\-\-driver simulator` only)
.TP
\fB\-\-sim\-tau\fR \fI<SIM_TAU>\fR [default: 2]
Simulator process time constant, in seconds (`\-\-driver simulator` only)
.TP
\fB\-\-sim\-dead\-time\fR \fI<SIM_DEAD_TIME>\fR [default: 5]
Simulator dead time, in seconds (`\-\-driver simulator` only)
.TP
\fB\-\-sim\-noise\fR \fI<SIM_NOISE>\fR [default: 0]
Simulator measurement noise amplitude (`\-\-driver simulator` only)
.TP
\fB\-\-sim\-seed\fR \fI<SIM_SEED>\fR [default: 0]
Simulator RNG seed, for reproducible noise (`\-\-driver simulator` only)
.TP
\fB\-\-sim\-initial\-pv\fR \fI<SIM_INITIAL_PV>\fR [default: 50]
Simulator initial PV (`\-\-driver simulator` only)
.TP
\fB\-\-sim\-initial\-mv\fR \fI<SIM_INITIAL_MV>\fR [default: 50]
Simulator initial MV (`\-\-driver simulator` only)
.TP
\fB\-\-pv\-range\-high\fR \fI<PV_RANGE_HIGH>\fR
Fixed PV range high, overriding a live tag read (legacy: the PV range "toggle tag/value" button). Required (defaults to 100.0) for `\-\-driver simulator`, which has no range tags at all
.TP
\fB\-\-pv\-range\-low\fR \fI<PV_RANGE_LOW>\fR
Fixed PV range low, overriding a live tag read
.TP
\fB\-\-mv\-range\-high\fR \fI<MV_RANGE_HIGH>\fR
Fixed MV range high, overriding a live tag read
.TP
\fB\-\-mv\-range\-low\fR \fI<MV_RANGE_LOW>\fR
Fixed MV range low, overriding a live tag read
.TP
\fB\-\-direction\fR \fI<DIRECTION>\fR
Fixed controller direction, overriding a live tag read
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
direct
.IP \(bu 2
reverse
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-notes\fR \fI<NOTES>\fR
Operator notes to attach to this run. Notes can be edited or cleared from the web GUI while the run is active or after it finishes
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Confirm an unattended PID write\-back. Required alongside `\-\-write\-pid` \-\- the command refuses to start otherwise \-\- since writing to a live loop with no human present must be an explicit, deliberate choice. Has no effect without `\-\-write\-pid`
.TP
\fB\-\-write\-pid\fR \fI<WRITE_PID>\fR
Non\-interactively write this response level\*(Aqs calculated PID parameters back to the DCS instead of prompting on stdin \-\- the flag that makes a scheduled/scripted tune able to actually update a loop with no one watching. Requires `\-\-yes`
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
aggressive
.IP \(bu 2
moderate
.IP \(bu 2
sluggish
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR [default: table]
How to print this run\*(Aqs final outcome line
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
table: Human\-readable text (default)
.IP \(bu 2
json: Pretty\-printed JSON. This is the external contract for scripted/scheduled consumers, so its shape must not change silently once shipped
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
